//* Finance Phase 1A — lifecycle for financial reference data (Currency,
//* PaymentProvider). Deliberately just ACTIVE/INACTIVE: reference rows are
//* never hard-deleted (historical financial records will point at them),
//* they're only retired from being selectable for NEW configuration.
enum FinanceReferenceStatus {
  ACTIVE
  INACTIVE
}

//* Finance Phase 1A — the discrete financial operations a PaymentProvider
//* implementation can support. A country may only enable an operation
//* whose configured provider declares the matching capability. Segregated
//* by operation (not one "supportsPayments" blob) because providers
//* genuinely differ — one may do card collection + bank payout only,
//* another mobile-money end to end.
enum PaymentProviderCapability {
  COLLECTION_CARD
  COLLECTION_MOBILE_MONEY
  COLLECTION_BANK_TRANSFER
  REFUND
  BANK_ACCOUNT_RESOLUTION
  PAYOUT_BANK
  PAYOUT_MOBILE_MONEY
  WEBHOOKS
}

//* Finance Phase 1B — which set of provider credentials an account uses.
//* NOT a deployment environment. The application's NODE_ENV decides which
//* is activatable: production => LIVE only, non-production => TEST only
//* (assertEnvironmentActivatable).
enum PaymentEnvironment {
  TEST
  LIVE
}

//* Finance Phase 1B — lifecycle of a country's financial configuration and
//* of each provider account. DRAFT = being set up, not operational.
//* ACTIVE = validated + explicitly activated. SUSPENDED = temporary halt,
//* reversible, blocks NEW operations only. DISABLED = retired, terminal,
//* existing records preserved. Raw status writes are never exposed — only
//* explicit activate/suspend/disable actions.
enum CountryFinancialConfigStatus {
  DRAFT
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  DISABLED
}

enum CountryProviderAccountStatus {
  DRAFT
